    "human_rct_r_rationale": "Empirical & Architectural Rationale for Mean R ~ 0.45 - 0.50 in Human RCTs: (1) Formulation: R = mlp(combined) * q_factor, where q_factor = 0.35 + 0.65 * (0.5 * qual + 0.5 * ctx). For human RCTs, qual ~ 0.90, ctx = 1.0 -> q_factor ~ 0.95. Sigmoid MLP outputs center around 0.48 - 0.50, yielding R ~ 0.45 - 0.48. (2) Convex Combination Safeguard: R acts as a gating weight: z_fused = (1 - R)*z_graph + R*z_contextual. If R approached 1.0, the model would completely throw away z_graph (the heterogeneous biological graph containing target CYP enzyme and transporter clearance pathway overlap). An intermediate R ~ 0.45 preserves molecular mechanism grounding while incorporating clinical text observations."
